 "human_notes": {
  "entry": [
   "There is NO dimension and NO portal. Alex's Caves adds five underground biomes to the Overworld, and the whole mod is gated behind FINDING them. Source rvUDlgjl2lk.",
   "The real entry step is a surface structure: small cabins that generate anywhere in the world. They contain alexscaves:cave_tablet (one per cave type), an alexscaves:cave_book, and most importantly an alexscaves:spelunkery_table.",
   "The Spelunkery Table is a WORD PUZZLE, not a crafting bench. You get five attempts to guess a word written in the Standard Galactic Alphabet; the first guess is always random, and a lens reveals which letter maps to which symbol. Solve it three times and you get an alexscaves:cave_codex for the cave you were searching.",
   "The codex updates your alexscaves:cave_book and produces an alexscaves:cave_map, which then searches your world and points you at an actual cave. Without this you are just digging at random.",
   "A quest chain for this mod should therefore start: find a cabin -> get alexscaves:spelunkery_table and an alexscaves:cave_tablet -> solve the puzzle -> alexscaves:cave_codex -> alexscaves:cave_map -> the biome."
  ],
  "boss_order": [
   "No linear boss ladder. The five biomes are independent and can be tackled in any order; difficulty, not a lock chain, is what separates them.",
   "The transcript names large threats per biome rather than gate bosses: alexscaves:tremorsaurus and alexscaves:tremorzilla in the Primordial Caves, alexscaves:magnetron and alexscaves:teletor in the Magnetic Caves, alexscaves:forsaken and alexscaves:vesper in the Forlorn Hollows, alexscaves:gammaroach and alexscaves:nucleeper in the Toxic Caves, alexscaves:deep_one with its knight and mage variants plus alexscaves:hullbreaker in the Abyssal Chasm.",
   "The alexscaves:abyssal_altar and alexscaves:pearl offerings to the deep ones are the closest thing to a ritual progression, and the transcript does not lay out its steps in order - do NOT invent them."
  ],
  "order": [
   "The five biomes are: Primordial Caves (dinosaurs), Magnetic Caves (galena and magnets), Forlorn Hollows (darkness), Toxic Caves (acid and radiation), Abyssal Chasm (deep underwater).",
   "Each has a hard prerequisite BEFORE you can usefully explore it, and that is the ordering that matters for a questbook:",
   "Forlorn Hollows: 'extremely dark and gloomy... shrouded by darkness' - the guide immediately puts on night vision. Bring it.",
   "Toxic Caves: bring a hazmat suit (alexscaves:hazmat_mask, alexscaves:hazmat_chestplate) before going, not after. It reduces the Irradiated effect AND the armour degradation from acid.",
   "Abyssal Chasm: you need the Deep Sight effect to see at all. The potion's only ingredient is alexscaves:lanternfish. Lanternfish rise to the surface at night, which is also how you FIND the Abyssal Chasm from above.",
   "Toxic Caves material chain: kill alexscaves:gammaroach for alexscaves:toxic_paste -> alexscaves:polymer_plate -> the hazmat set."
  ],
  "gates": [
   "HARD GATE on the whole mod: no alexscaves:cave_map means no reliable way to find any of the five biomes.",
   "Abyssal Chasm is unusable without Deep Sight; the guide treats it as mandatory equipment.",
   "alexscaves:diving_helmet and the rest of the diving set CANNOT BE CRAFTED. They only drop from a drone mob that spawns in the Abyssal Chasm, and are repaired with a copper ingot. Do not write a crafting quest for them."
  ],
  "traps": [
   "Merely HOLDING alexscaves:waste_drum or alexscaves:unrefined_waste in your inventory irradiates you - no contact needed. The guide calls this out as a surprise.",
   "Irradiated turns your hearts yellow and PREVENTS ALL NATURAL HEALING while it lasts.",
   "Destroying a alexscaves:waste_drum in lava explodes and irradiates you.",
   "alexscaves:acid burns dropped items like lava and degrades armour, though it deals slightly less damage.",
   "alexscaves:nucleeper explodes like a creeper and 'nothing can really stop that' once it starts - except a alexscaves:raycat, which reverses the explosion. A raycat also drains Irradiated out of you within 28 blocks.",
   "The guide flags alexscaves:radgill HP as buggy at time of filming - treat exact combat numbers as unreliable."
